<Project>
  <!-- Deliberately does NOT import the repo-root Directory.Build.props.
       MSBuild walks up and stops at the FIRST Directory.Build.props it finds, so
       this file shields SBPR.Trailborne.Core from the root's SbprValidateSdkPaths
       target, which hard-errors unless the Valheim managed-assembly + BepInEx paths
       are set.

       The Core is engine-free BY DESIGN (arch review P0): it references no Valheim /
       BepInEx / Unity / Harmony assemblies, so it must NOT inherit the SDK-path
       requirement — it has to compile headless in CI and on any dev box without the
       Valheim SDK fetched (exactly like the tests/ subtree, which uses the same
       shielding trick). The shipping shell at src/SBPR.Trailborne/ is a SIBLING
       subtree and still finds the root props unchanged, so this override does not
       affect the mod build.

       This file is intentionally near-empty: its mere PRESENCE is the shield. -->
</Project>
